   "changelog_1_7": "Louisville KY ratified as the 10th canonical cluster (entry-phase), closing the split this file itself flagged 2026-07-16 (known_provisional_addition_2026_07_16): acquisition-underwriting had been scoring Louisville as an entry cluster since v3.4 (2026-06-22) while this file — the canonical cross-skill source of truth — did not recognize it, leaving deal-comparison, market-monitor, rent-comp, and daily-brief blind to it. Gabriel ratified it in-turn 2026-08-05. Every field in the new cluster record is sourced from acquisition-underwriting's own June-2026 rationale (UPS Worldport anchor, GE Appliances $490M reshoring, Riverport pricing 40% below MSA average, adjacency to the Indiana established cluster) — nothing new was researched for this ratification. Hard cost is a PROXY off Indianapolis (nearest cluster, per the skill's own adjacency framing) pending a real quote; vacancy/absorption/construction-pipeline metrics were never pulled and are left null rather than guessed. Ruling 3 (no satellite eligibility until a closed deal) applies to Louisville exactly as it does to the other three entry clusters. KY added to acceptable_states as a target-activity state (ORA holds no property there). The Notion Acquisition Pipeline Tracker \"Market\" select (bcfe4a03) and Owner Outreach Queue \"Metro\" select (caa809b7) were updated the same session (2026-08-05) via notion-update-data-source — Louisville KY / Louisville added as options, every pre-existing option's UUID verified unchanged (only the new option was appended), so no historical row value was disturbed. All five listed consumers plus both Notion selects are now at parity. No governor, scorecard weight, or Stage 1 floor changed — this is a market-set membership decision, the same class of change Grand Rapids/Richmond/Des Moines were on 2026-05-30.",
   "changelog_1_8": "Same-day wording-only follow-up to 1.7 — no market data, scores, or fields changed. The changelog_1_7 entry said the Notion Acquisition Pipeline Tracker \"Market\" select and Owner Outreach Queue \"Metro\" select still needed Louisville added manually; that update landed later the same session (notion-update-data-source against collection://bcfe4a03... and collection://caa809b7..., every pre-existing option UUID verified unchanged, only the new option appended). Text corrected to reflect completion rather than leave a stale \"not done here\" note in ratified doctrine.",
   "changelog_1_9": "Louisville KY: replacement_cost block DELETED (Gabriel, 2026-08-12). It carried hard_cost_psf 143.46 as an INDIANAPOLIS proxy, plus the claim that \"Louisville is NOT in the C&W guide and has no independent hard-cost pull\". BOTH WERE WRONG. Louisville IS in the C&W 2025 guide; its small-tier figure is $135.28/SF, present all along in the repo's own 45-market extract at scheduled-tasks/ora-deal-sourcing-scan/skills/cw-2025-construction-costs.json. That sourced figure now drives a real RCT v03 row in acquisition-underwriting (Louisville KY | 237.07 | 263.41 | 289.75 | 135.28), so no proxy is needed and the stale block was removed rather than corrected — leaving it would have been a third denominator location. Louisville is now the ONLY cluster with no replacement_cost block. The other nine KEEP theirs by decision (Gabriel, 2026-08-12): their figures are correct and match the C&W hard costs behind RCT v03, and they carry provenance found nowhere else (2024 comparatives, YoY %, land $/acre, small-bay extrapolations). Those nine are PROVENANCE, NEVER a denominator — this file's operative benchmark was RETIRED 2026-07-14 and RCT v03 in acquisition-underwriting is the only one. No market data, scores, submarkets or fields changed for any other cluster.",
-  "changelog_1_10": "Two corrections from the 2026-08-15 ora-skill-text-audit remediation pass (findings F4-F6 + F1-F3 wrap-up), no market data, scores, or governors changed. (1) The `consumers` array's `rent-comp` entry (Oxford Market Benchmarks) was stale — that skill was retired 2026-08-05 and its comp-grid function absorbed into acquisition-underwriting's COMP GRID DISCIPLINE section 2026-08-12; the entry is repointed there, distinguished from the pre-existing 'Markets hard filter' acquisition-underwriting entry above it. (2) changelog_1_7's claim \"All five listed consumers plus both Notion selects are now at parity\" was FALSE at the time it was written and stayed false for 10 days: `market-monitor`, `deal-comparison`, and `daily-brief` had NOT actually been updated with the Louisville KY entry-phase profile/list entries (confirmed by direct read 2026-08-15) — only acquisition-underwriting itself and the two Notion selects were current. All three skill files are fixed as of this remediation pass; full parity across every listed consumer now genuinely holds."
